IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `maia-dates`
IMPORT `maia-claims`

-- Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 (NSW) -- Part 3 (statutory benefits), with the definitions it rests on (ss 1.4,
-- 1.6, 1.7, 1.8-1.10) and Schedule 1 (who is an earner), from the seat of the person injured in a motor accident.
--
-- SEAT: the injured person (for funeral expenses, s 3.4, the person who pays for the funeral or the legal personal
-- representative of the person who died). Every exported question is one that person would ask: "Are statutory
-- benefits payable to me?", "Who pays them?", "Am I an earner?", "Which entitlement period am I in?", "Am I entitled to
-- weekly payments for this day?", "How much is my weekly payment?", "How much notice must my insurer give before
-- stopping them?", "Must I tell my insurer I am back at work?", "Must a finding of contributory negligence be made
-- against me?", "Can I get statutory benefits for this treatment and care expense?", "... for paying someone to do the
-- domestic services I used to do?", "Can I get funeral expenses?". The insurer, the Authority and the Commission get no
-- seat: what they decide is asked as a fact or answered conditionally.
--
-- REGULATION. The Motor Accident Injuries Regulation 2017 (deposited beside the Act, version as at 22 September 2023)
-- is brought in where it sets Part 3's numbers and terms: cl 4 (threshold injuries, s 1.6(4)), cl 7 (the minimum weekly
-- amount, s 3.10) and, through maia-claims.l4, cl 8A (s 6.13(2)). It prescribes no serious driving offence (s 3.37(5)),
-- no fixed contributory negligence percentage (s 3.38(4)) and no other period for ss 3.14 or 3.15.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, a
-- condition introduced by "if", "only if" or "where", a flat "not entitled", "not payable" or "does not apply", a
-- period the text fixes), or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given; each NOTHING carries a
-- "NOTHING-kind" comment. A number question answers NOTHING where the Act does not give a number on the facts.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 1 April 2023; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 -- Part 3 Statutory benefits`

§§ `The nouns`

-- s 3.36 and s 3.36(5): the injured person's part in a vehicle involved in the accident.
DECLARE `My role in a vehicle` IS ONE OF
    `I was the driver of a vehicle involved`
    `I owned a vehicle involved but was not driving it`
    `I was neither the owner nor the driver of a vehicle involved`

-- s 3.5 "first entitlement period ... means the period of 13 weeks that starts on the day after the day of the motor
-- accident"; "second entitlement period ... means the period of 65 weeks that starts on the day after the end of the
-- first entitlement period"; s 3.8 "after the end of the second entitlement period".
DECLARE `The entitlement period` IS ONE OF
    `the first entitlement period (weeks 1 to 13)`
    `the second entitlement period (weeks 14 to 78)`
    `after the second entitlement period (after week 78)`
    `not after the day of the accident`

-- s 3.2: who pays.
DECLARE `The payer of statutory benefits` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer of the motor vehicle`
    `the insurer of the at-fault motor vehicle`
    `the Nominal Defendant`
    `the Nominal Defendant, on behalf of the non-licensed insurer`
    `a licensed insurer, under arrangements the Authority approved`
    `the Lifetime Care and Support Authority`

-- s 3.19(4)-(7): why the weekly payments are being stopped or reduced.
DECLARE `Why my weekly payments are stopping or going down` IS ONE OF
    `I returned to or started work, or my earnings from work changed`
    `a lower rate applies because an earlier period ended`
    `my weekly payments are being suspended`
    `another reason`

-- s 3.24(1), 3.25: the treatment and care expense asked about.
DECLARE `The treatment and care expense` IS ONE OF
    `the cost of treatment and care`
    `my travel and accommodation to get treatment and care`
    `a parent's or carer's travel and accommodation to go with me to treatment and care`
    `attendant care services given to me that I have not paid and need not pay for`
    `some other expense`

-- s 3.26(5) "dependants means (a) such of the following persons as are wholly or partly dependent on the claimant at
-- the time of the motor accident -- (i) [spouse] (ii) a de facto partner (iii) a child, grandchild, sibling, uncle,
-- aunt, niece, nephew, parent or grandparent ... (iv) any other person who is a member of the claimant's household,
-- and (b) any unborn child of the claimant ... at the time of the motor accident and who is born after that time".
DECLARE `The dependant` IS ONE OF
    `my spouse, de facto partner or relative, who depended on me at the time of the accident`
    `another member of my household, who depended on me at the time of the accident`
    `my child, unborn at the time of the accident and born after it`
    `none of these`

-- s 3.4(1): the person asking about funeral expenses.
DECLARE `My position after the death` IS ONE OF
    `I am the legal personal representative of the person who died`
    `I paid or must pay the funeral expenses, and there is no legal personal representative`
    `I paid or must pay the funeral expenses, but there is a legal personal representative`
    `none of these`

-- s 3.4(2), (3): where the body is taken.
DECLARE `Where the body is taken` IS ONE OF
    `an appropriate place to prepare it for burial or cremation`
    `the usual place of residence of the person who died`
    `the country outside Australia where the person who died usually lived`
    `somewhere else`

§§ `s 1.6 and Regulation cl 4 -- threshold injuries`

-- s 1.6(1) "a threshold injury is, subject to this section, one or more of the following -- (a) a soft tissue injury,
-- (b) a psychological or psychiatric injury that is not a recognised psychiatric illness." (2) "A soft tissue injury is
-- ... an injury to tissue that connects, supports or surrounds other structures or organs of the body (such as muscles,
-- tendons, ligaments, menisci, cartilage, fascia, fibrous tissues, fat, blood vessels and synovial membranes), but not
-- an injury to nerves or a complete or partial rupture of tendons, ligaments, menisci or cartilage." Regulation cl 4(1)
-- "An injury to a spinal nerve root that manifests in neurological signs (other than radiculopathy) is included as a
-- soft tissue injury"; (2) acute stress disorder and adjustment disorder (as in DSM-5) are included as threshold
-- injuries. "Recognised psychiatric illness" is a borrowed term, asked through the choice of injury. A definition
-- ("is"): an injury outside it is JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `The injury` IS ONE OF
    `an injury to soft tissue (muscle, tendon, ligament, meniscus, cartilage, fascia, fibrous tissue, fat, blood vessel, synovial membrane) that is not a rupture`
    `a complete or partial rupture of a tendon, ligament, meniscus or cartilage`
    `an injury to a nerve, other than a spinal nerve root`
    `an injury to a spinal nerve root showing neurological signs other than radiculopathy`
    `an injury to a spinal nerve root with radiculopathy`
    `acute stress disorder or adjustment disorder`
    `another psychological or psychiatric injury that is not a recognised psychiatric illness`
    `a recognised psychiatric illness`
    `a fracture, or another injury not listed`

@export Is this injury of mine a "threshold injury", which limits my statutory benefits after 52 weeks (s 1.6; Regulation cl 4)?
GIVEN `the injury` IS A `The injury` @desc The injury. One of: "an injury to soft tissue (muscle, tendon, ligament, meniscus, cartilage, fascia, fibrous tissue, fat, blood vessel, synovial membrane) that is not a rupture", "a complete or partial rupture of a tendon, ligament, meniscus or cartilage", "an injury to a nerve, other than a spinal nerve root", "an injury to a spinal nerve root showing neurological signs other than radiculopathy", "an injury to a spinal nerve root with radiculopathy", "acute stress disorder or adjustment disorder", "another psychological or psychiatric injury that is not a recognised psychiatric illness", "a recognised psychiatric illness", "a fracture, or another injury not listed"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my injury a threshold injury` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the injury`
    WHEN `an injury to soft tissue (muscle, tendon, ligament, meniscus, cartilage, fascia, fibrous tissue, fat, blood vessel, synovial membrane) that is not a rupture` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an injury to a spinal nerve root showing neurological signs other than radiculopathy` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `acute stress disorder or adjustment disorder` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another psychological or psychiatric injury that is not a recognised psychiatric illness` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Thresholds shared by several sections`

-- ss 3.11(2), 3.28(2), 3.36(4) "A motor accident was caused mostly by the fault of a person if the contributory
-- negligence of the person ... was greater than 61%." "Wholly" is 100%, which is also greater than 61%.
GIVEN `the share of fault` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accident was caused wholly or mostly by my fault` `the share of fault` IF `the share of fault` GREATER THAN 61

-- s 1.7(2): physical and psychological or psychiatric impairment are assessed separately and not added; the person is
-- over the impairment threshold if either is greater than 10%.
GIVEN `the physical impairment` IS A NUMBER, `the psychological impairment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my permanent impairment is greater than 10%` `the physical impairment` `the psychological impairment` IF
        `the physical impairment` GREATER THAN 10
    OR `the psychological impairment` GREATER THAN 10

-- s 3.5: which entitlement period a day falls in. Day 1 is the day after the accident; days 1-91 are the 13 weeks of
-- the first period; days 92-546 the 65 weeks of the second.
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE, `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The entitlement period`
`the entitlement period of` `the accident day` `the day asked about` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day number` AT MOST 0 THEN `not after the day of the accident`
           IF `the day number` AT MOST 91 THEN `the first entitlement period (weeks 1 to 13)`
           IF `the day number` AT MOST 546 THEN `the second entitlement period (weeks 14 to 78)`
           OTHERWISE `after the second entitlement period (after week 78)`
    WHERE
        `the day number` MEANS `the days from` `the accident day` `to` `the day asked about`

§§ `ss 1.8-1.10, 3.1, 3.35(1), 3.36, 3.37 -- are statutory benefits payable at all`

-- s 1.8 "This Act does not apply to or in respect of a motor accident occurring before the commencement of this Act."
-- s 1.9(1) "applies ... only if the death or injury is a result of and is caused ... during (a) the driving of the
-- vehicle, or (b) a collision, or action taken to avoid a collision, with the vehicle, or (c) the vehicle's running out
-- of control, or (d) a dangerous situation caused by [any of those]". s 1.9(2) "does not apply in respect of an injury
-- that arises gradually from a series of incidents". s 1.10(1) "is limited to death or injury that (a) results from a
-- motor accident for which the vehicle has motor accident insurance cover, or (b) gives rise to a work injury claim".
-- s 3.1(1) "If the death of or injury to a person results from a motor accident in this State, statutory benefits are
-- payable"; (2) whether or not anyone was at fault, "even if" the injured person was. s 3.35(1) "not entitled to
-- statutory benefits under this Part if compensation under the Workers Compensation Act 1987 ... is payable". s 3.36(1)
-- "not payable ... in respect of the death of or injury to a person resulting wholly or mostly from the fault of the
-- person as the owner or driver of a motor vehicle ... if the vehicle was an uninsured vehicle"; (5) "does not apply to
-- a person who was the driver ... if (a) the driver was driving ... with the authority of the owner or had reasonable
-- grounds for believing ... and (b) the driver did not have any reasonable grounds for believing that the motor vehicle
-- was an uninsured vehicle". s 3.37(1) "not payable to an injured person after the person has been charged with or
-- convicted of a serious driving offence that was related to the motor accident"; (2) unless acquitted or the
-- proceedings discontinued (then payable from the charge date).
GIVEN `in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `caused during driving or a collision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arose gradually` IS A BOOLEAN
      `insurance cover` IS A BOOLEAN
      `work injury claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `workers compensation payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `role` IS A `My role in a vehicle`
      `fault` IS A NUMBER
      `uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `grounds to believe uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN
      `charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acquitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Part 3 gate` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `in New South Wales`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `after commencement`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `caused during driving or a collision`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `arose gradually` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT (`insurance cover` OR `work injury claim`)) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `workers compensation payable` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the s 3.36 bar` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `charged` AND (NOT `acquitted`) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `an owner or driver` MEANS
            CONSIDER `role`
            WHEN `I was neither the owner nor the driver of a vehicle involved` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the s 3.36(5) driver` MEANS
            CONSIDER `role`
            WHEN `I was the driver of a vehicle involved` THEN `authority` AND (NOT `grounds to believe uninsured`)
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `the s 3.36 bar` MEANS
                `an owner or driver`
            AND `the accident was caused wholly or mostly by my fault` `fault`
            AND `uninsured`
            AND (NOT `the s 3.36(5) driver`)

@export Are statutory benefits (weekly payments, treatment and care, funeral expenses) payable to me at all for my injury from a motor accident (ss 1.8-1.10, 3.1, 3.35(1), 3.36, 3.37)?
GIVEN `the accident happened in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accident happened in New South Wales
      `the accident happened on or after the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened on or after the day this Act commenced (the deposited text does not give the day; its transitional provisions point to 1 December 2017)
      `the injury was caused during the driving or a collision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was caused during the driving of a vehicle, a collision with it (or action taken to avoid one), the vehicle running out of control, or a dangerous situation caused by any of those
      `the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury arose gradually from a series of incidents rather than from one accident
      `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle had cover: a NSW green slip (third-party policy), an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme, Commonwealth ownership, or a right of action against the Nominal Defendant (for example, an unidentified or uninsured vehicle)
      `the injury gives rise to a work injury claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a worker injured through the negligence of your employer (a work injury claim under Part 5 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987), other than a coal miner
      `workers compensation is payable to me for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether workers compensation under the Workers Compensation Act 1987 is payable to you for this injury (for example, your workers compensation claim was accepted)
      `my role` IS A `My role in a vehicle` @desc Your part in a vehicle involved. One of: "I was the driver of a vehicle involved", "I owned a vehicle involved but was not driving it", "I was neither the owner nor the driver of a vehicle involved"
      `my share of the fault` IS A NUMBER @desc Your own share of the fault for the accident, as a percentage from 0 to 100 (your contributory negligence; 100 if it was wholly your fault)
      `that vehicle was uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you owned or drove a vehicle involved: whether it had no NSW green slip where one was required, no interstate or Commonwealth compulsory cover, and was not owned by the Commonwealth
      `I drove with the owner's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver: whether you drove with the owner's authority, or believed on reasonable grounds that you had it
      `I had reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver: whether you had any reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured
      `I have been charged with a serious driving offence related to the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with or convicted of a serious driving offence (a major offence under the Road Transport Act 2013, or one the regulations prescribe) about your driving of a vehicle involved in the accident
      `the charge ended in acquittal or was discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were acquitted, or the proceedings were discontinued (other than on a plea of guilty to another serious driving offence that contributed to your injury)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Are statutory benefits payable to me` MEANS
    `the Part 3 gate` `the accident happened in New South Wales` `the accident happened on or after the Act commenced` `the injury was caused during the driving or a collision` `the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents` `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover` `the injury gives rise to a work injury claim` `workers compensation is payable to me for the injury` `my role` `my share of the fault` `that vehicle was uninsured` `I drove with the owner's authority` `I had reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured` `I have been charged with a serious driving offence related to the accident` `the charge ended in acquittal or was discontinued`

§§ `s 3.2 -- who pays`

-- s 3.2(2) "(a) if the motor accident concerned involved only 1 motor vehicle with motor accident insurance cover--the
-- insurer of the motor vehicle, or (b) if the motor accident concerned involved more than 1 motor vehicle--the insurer
-- of the at-fault motor vehicle, or (c) in any other case--the Nominal Defendant." (3) treatment and care provided more
-- than 5 years after the accident: the Lifetime Care and Support Authority. (4) the at-fault vehicle is the one whose
-- use caused the injury, or that contributed most. (6) a non-licensed insurer: the Nominal Defendant pays on its behalf
-- unless the Authority approves arrangements with a licensed insurer; (7) if its policy does not cover statutory
-- benefits, the Nominal Defendant is the relevant insurer. s 3.45(2): the Lifetime Care and Support Authority may by
-- agreement take over treatment and care within the 5 years. Fork F5: (a) is read as one vehicle involved, which had
-- cover; where the at-fault vehicle of several had no cover, (b) has no insurer to name and the Nominal Defendant is
-- taken (as the Act's note says).
@export Who pays my statutory benefits (s 3.2, s 3.45(2))?
GIVEN `the number of motor vehicles involved` IS A NUMBER @desc How many motor vehicles were involved in the accident
      `the vehicle had motor accident insurance cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If one vehicle was involved: whether it had motor accident insurance cover (a green slip, or interstate or Commonwealth cover). If more than one: whether the at-fault vehicle (the one whose use caused your injury, or contributed most) had it
      `that insurer is licensed in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer of the at-fault vehicle is a licensed insurer under this Act (answer yes if you do not know of any interstate or other insurer)
      `that insurer's policy covers statutory benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the at-fault vehicle's insurer is not licensed: whether its policy insures against a liability to pay statutory benefits
      `the Authority approved arrangements with a licensed insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the at-fault vehicle's insurer is not licensed: whether the Authority gave written approval for it to arrange for a licensed insurer to pay
      `I am asking about treatment and care given more than 5 years after the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are asking about payment for treatment and care provided more than 5 years after the accident
      `the Lifetime Care and Support Authority agreed to take over my treatment and care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Lifetime Care and Support Authority has agreed with the insurer to take over payment for your treatment and care (s 3.45(2)), and you are asking about treatment and care
GIVETH A MAYBE `The payer of statutory benefits`
`Who pays my statutory benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I am asking about treatment and care given more than 5 years after the accident` THEN JUST `the Lifetime Care and Support Authority`
           IF `the Lifetime Care and Support Authority agreed to take over my treatment and care` THEN JUST `the Lifetime Care and Support Authority`
           IF `the number of motor vehicles involved` LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (no vehicle: not a motor accident; the text is silent)
           IF `the number of motor vehicles involved` EQUALS 1 THEN
               IF `the vehicle had motor accident insurance cover`
               THEN JUST `the insurer of the motor vehicle`
               ELSE JUST `the Nominal Defendant`
           IF (NOT `the vehicle had motor accident insurance cover`) THEN JUST `the Nominal Defendant`
           IF `that insurer is licensed in New South Wales` THEN JUST `the insurer of the at-fault motor vehicle`
           IF (NOT `that insurer's policy covers statutory benefits`) THEN JUST `the Nominal Defendant`
           IF `the Authority approved arrangements with a licensed insurer` THEN JUST `a licensed insurer, under arrangements the Authority approved`
           OTHERWISE JUST `the Nominal Defendant, on behalf of the non-licensed insurer`

§§ `Schedule 1 -- am I an earner`

-- Sch 1 cl 2 "A person who is injured as a result of a motor accident is an earner if the person is at least 15 years
-- of age and who (a) was employed or self-employed ... (i) at any time during the 8 weeks immediately preceding the motor
-- accident, or (ii) during a period or periods equal to at least 13 weeks during the year immediately preceding ..., or
-- (iii) ... at least 26 weeks during the 2 years immediately preceding ..., and, at the date of the motor accident, had
-- not retired permanently from all employment, or (b) ... had entered into an arrangement ... to undertake employment,
-- or ... to commence business as a self-employed person, at a particular time and place, or (c) was, immediately before
-- the motor accident, receiving a weekly payment or other payment in respect of loss of earnings under this Act or the
-- Workers Compensation Act 1987." An "if" condition: otherwise JUST FALSE, except that a full-time student may be
-- taken to be an earner later under cl 5 (NOTHING here, cl 5 depending on when the course would have been completed).
@export Was I an "earner" when I was injured, so that I can get weekly payments in the first 78 weeks (Schedule 1, clause 2)?
GIVEN `my age at the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the day of the accident
      `I worked at any time in the 8 weeks before the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed or self-employed (full-time or not) at any time in the 8 weeks just before the accident
      `the weeks I worked in the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in total you were employed or self-employed during the year just before the accident
      `the weeks I worked in the 2 years before the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in total you were employed or self-employed during the 2 years just before the accident
      `I had retired permanently from all employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of the accident, you had retired permanently from all employment
      `I had arranged to start a job or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before the accident, you had arranged (even informally) to start employment, or a business as a self-employed person, at a particular time and place
      `I was receiving payments for loss of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before the accident, you were receiving weekly or other payments for loss of earnings under this Act or the Workers Compensation Act 1987
      `I was a full-time student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a full-time student at the time of the accident
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I an earner` MEANS
    IF `my age at the accident` AT LEAST 15
       AND (    (`recent work` AND (NOT `I had retired permanently from all employment`))
             OR `I had arranged to start a job or business`
             OR `I was receiving payments for loss of earnings`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `I was a full-time student`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (Sch 1 cl 5 may make a full-time student an earner from when the course would have been completed; points outside the facts asked)
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `recent work` MEANS
                `I worked at any time in the 8 weeks before the accident`
            OR `the weeks I worked in the year before the accident` AT LEAST 13
            OR `the weeks I worked in the 2 years before the accident` AT LEAST 26

§§ `s 3.5 -- the entitlement periods`

@export Which entitlement period for weekly payments does this day fall in: the first (weeks 1 to 13 after my accident), the second (weeks 14 to 78), or after the second (s 3.5)?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want to know about
GIVETH A `The entitlement period`
`Which entitlement period is this day in` MEANS `the entitlement period of` `the day of my accident` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `ss 3.6-3.13, 3.21, 3.40, 6.13(2) -- am I entitled to weekly payments for this day`

-- s 3.11(1) "not entitled to weekly payments ... for any period of loss of earnings or earning capacity that occurs
-- more than 52 weeks after the motor accident concerned if (a) the motor accident was caused wholly or mostly by the
-- fault of the person, or (b) the person's only injuries resulting from the motor accident were threshold injuries."
-- Sch 4 cl 15: the 2022 amendments ("Statutory benefits after 26 weeks") do not apply to an accident before they
-- commenced; the earlier text (26 weeks) is not deposited, so between 26 and 52 weeks for such an accident the answer
-- is NOTHING (fork F6). JUST TRUE means the bar applies.
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE, `the day asked about` IS A DATE, `fault` IS A NUMBER
      `only threshold injuries` IS A BOOLEAN, `the 2022 amendments apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the s 3.11 bar` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the condition`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the day asked about` `is more than` 52 `weeks after` `the accident day` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF (NOT `the 2022 amendments apply`) AND (`the day asked about` `is more than` 26 `weeks after` `the accident day`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: the pre-2022 text)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the condition` MEANS `the accident was caused wholly or mostly by my fault` `fault` OR `only threshold injuries`

-- s 3.12(2) "(a) 104 weeks, unless the person's injury is the subject of a pending claim for damages ..., (b) 156
-- weeks if ... such a pending claim and the degree of any permanent impairment ... is not greater than 10%, (c) 260
-- weeks if ... such a pending claim and the degree of permanent impairment ... is greater than 10%." (3) the period
-- ends if the pending claim is withdrawn, settled or finally determined after 104 weeks: asked as "pending on the day
-- asked about" (fork F7).
GIVEN `pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `over 10%` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum weekly payment period in weeks` MEANS
    IF (NOT `pending`) THEN 104
    ELSE IF `over 10%` THEN 260 ELSE 156

-- s 3.13 "(1) If the motor accident ... happens before the person reaches the retiring age, a weekly payment ... is not
-- to be made ... for any ... period ... occurring after the first anniversary of the date on which the person reaches
-- the retiring age. (2) If the motor accident ... happens on or after the person reaches the retiring age, ... not ...
-- more than 12 months after the motor accident occurs." Retiring age (the age pension age under the Social Security
-- Act 1991 (Cth)) is a borrowed term: the day it is reached is asked. JUST TRUE means the bar applies.
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE, `the day asked about` IS A DATE, `the retiring age day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 3.13 bar` MEANS
    IF `the accident day` `is before` `the retiring age day`
    THEN `the day asked about` `is after` (`the retiring age day` `plus months` 12)
    ELSE `the day asked about` `is after` (`the accident day` `plus months` 12)

@export Am I entitled to weekly payments of statutory benefits for my loss of earnings on this day (ss 3.6-3.8, 3.11-3.13, 3.21, 3.35, 3.36, 3.37, 3.40, 6.13(2))?
GIVEN `the accident happened in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accident happened in New South Wales
      `the accident happened on or after the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened on or after the day this Act commenced (the deposited text does not give the day; its transitional provisions point to 1 December 2017)
      `the injury was caused during the driving or a collision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was caused during the driving of a vehicle, a collision with it (or action taken to avoid one), the vehicle running out of control, or a dangerous situation caused by any of those
      `the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury arose gradually from a series of incidents rather than from one accident
      `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle had cover: a NSW green slip, an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme, Commonwealth ownership, or a right of action against the Nominal Defendant
      `the injury gives rise to a work injury claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a worker injured through the negligence of your employer (a work injury claim), other than a coal miner
      `workers compensation is payable to me for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether workers compensation under the Workers Compensation Act 1987 is payable to you for this injury
      `my role` IS A `My role in a vehicle` @desc Your part in a vehicle involved. One of: "I was the driver of a vehicle involved", "I owned a vehicle involved but was not driving it", "I was neither the owner nor the driver of a vehicle involved"
      `my share of the fault` IS A NUMBER @desc Your own share of the fault for the accident, as a percentage from 0 to 100 (your contributory negligence; 100 if it was wholly your fault)
      `that vehicle was uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you owned or drove a vehicle involved: whether it had no NSW green slip where one was required, no interstate or Commonwealth compulsory cover, and was not owned by the Commonwealth
      `I drove with the owner's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver: whether you drove with the owner's authority, or believed on reasonable grounds that you had it
      `I had reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver: whether you had any reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured
      `I have been charged with a serious driving offence related to the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the day you are asking about, you had been charged with or convicted of a serious driving offence about your driving of a vehicle involved in the accident
      `the charge ended in acquittal or was discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were acquitted, or the proceedings were discontinued (other than on a plea of guilty to another serious driving offence that contributed to your injury)
      `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day of loss of earnings you are asking about
      `I was an earner when injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were an "earner" when injured (worked out by the question "Was I an earner")
      `I have a loss of earnings or earning capacity on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of the injury, you have a total or partial loss of earnings (in weeks 1 to 78) or of earning capacity (after week 78) on that day
      `my age on that day` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the day you are asking about
      `my only injuries were threshold injuries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your only injuries from the accident were threshold injuries (worked out by the question "Is my injury a threshold injury"): soft tissue injuries, or psychological or psychiatric injuries that are not a recognised psychiatric illness
      `my claim for damages is pending on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on that day, you have a claim for damages for this injury that is pending (not withdrawn, settled or finally determined), whether or not the insurer accepted liability
      `my physical permanent impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of permanent impairment from your physical injuries, as a percentage (0 if none has been assessed)
      `my psychological permanent impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of permanent impairment from your psychological or psychiatric injuries, as a percentage, assessed separately (0 if none)
      `the day I reach retiring age` IS A DATE @desc The day you reached, or will reach, the age at which you could get the age pension under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth)
      `I live outside Australia on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were residing outside Australia on that day
      `my loss of earning capacity has been found likely to be permanent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you live outside Australia: whether the insurer or the Personal Injury Commission has determined that your loss of earning capacity is likely to be permanent
      `I have established my identity and continuing loss as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you live outside Australia: whether you have established your identity and the continuing loss as the Motor Accident Guidelines require
      `I have recovered damages for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have recovered damages for this injury from the owner or driver of a vehicle (through their insurer) or from your employer
      `the day I made my claim for statutory benefits` IS A DATE @desc The day you made (or will make) your claim for statutory benefits
      `I gave a full and satisfactory explanation for the late claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claimed more than 28 days after the accident: whether you gave a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay (taken to be one if the insurer did not reject it within 14 days of receiving it)
      `my weekly payments are suspended on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your weekly payments are suspended on that day for a failure the Act lets the insurer suspend for (not giving a medical certificate or authority, s 3.14; a certificate of fitness, s 3.15; refusing required treatment, s 3.17; not minimising loss, s 6.5; a direction, s 6.6; an examination, s 6.27)
      `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your accident happened on or after the day the changes made by the Motor Accident Injuries Amendment Act 2022 commenced (the deposited text does not give that day)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to weekly payments for this day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the gate` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the period` EQUALS `not after the day of the accident` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `after week 78` AND (NOT (`my age on that day` AT LEAST 18 OR `I was an earner when injured`)) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the s 3.11 bar` `the day of my accident` `the day I am asking about` `my share of the fault` `my only injuries were threshold injuries` `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the day I am asking about` `is more than` (`the maximum weekly payment period in weeks` `my claim for damages is pending on that day` `over the impairment threshold`) `weeks after` `the day of my accident` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the s 3.13 bar` `the day of my accident` `the day I am asking about` `the day I reach retiring age` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `I live outside Australia on that day` AND (NOT (`my loss of earning capacity has been found likely to be permanent` AND `I have established my identity and continuing loss as required`)) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `I have recovered damages for this injury` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the s 6.13(2) bar` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `my weekly payments are suspended on that day` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the s 3.11 bar` `the day of my accident` `the day I am asking about` `my share of the fault` `my only injuries were threshold injuries` `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: the pre-2022 text)
           IF (NOT `I have a loss of earnings or earning capacity on that day`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited by its own wording, "suffers a total or partial loss"; the case falls outside it)
           IF (NOT `after week 78`) AND (NOT `I was an earner when injured`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited by its own wording, "An earner who ..."; fork F8)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the gate` MEANS `the Part 3 gate` `the accident happened in New South Wales` `the accident happened on or after the Act commenced` `the injury was caused during the driving or a collision` `the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents` `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover` `the injury gives rise to a work injury claim` `workers compensation is payable to me for the injury` `my role` `my share of the fault` `that vehicle was uninsured` `I drove with the owner's authority` `I had reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured` `I have been charged with a serious driving offence related to the accident` `the charge ended in acquittal or was discontinued`
        `the period` MEANS `the entitlement period of` `the day of my accident` `the day I am asking about`
        `after week 78` MEANS `the period` EQUALS `after the second entitlement period (after week 78)`
        `over the impairment threshold` MEANS `my permanent impairment is greater than 10%` `my physical permanent impairment` `my psychological permanent impairment`
        -- s 6.13(2) and Regulation cl 8A (in maia-claims.l4): before a claim made more than 28 days after the
        -- accident, weekly payments are not payable unless the Regulation permits it.
        `the s 6.13(2) bar` MEANS
                `the day I am asking about` `is before` `the day I made my claim for statutory benefits`
            AND (NOT (`weekly payments are payable for the time before the claim` `the day of my accident` `the day I made my claim for statutory benefits` `I gave a full and satisfactory explanation for the late claim`))

§§ `ss 3.6-3.10, 3.38 -- how much is the weekly payment`

-- s 3.6(2) "at the rate of 95% of the difference between the person's pre-accident weekly earnings and the person's
-- post-accident earning capacity (if any) or post-accident earnings, whichever is the greater"; s 3.7(2) and 3.8(2):
-- 80% for a total loss, 85% for a partial loss (after week 78, of pre-accident earning capacity). (3) "not to exceed the
-- maximum weekly statutory benefits amount less the person's post-accident earning capacity (if any) or post-accident
-- earnings, whichever is the greater". (4) "not to be less than the minimum weekly statutory benefits amount or the
-- person's pre-accident weekly earnings [after week 78: earning capacity], whichever is the lesser."
-- A total loss is read as nothing left: post-accident earning capacity and earnings both 0 (fork F9). Where the
-- minimum in (4) is above the ceiling in (3), the two cannot both hold and the Act does not say which wins: NOTHING
-- (fork F10). Where there is no loss (the post-accident amount is at least the pre-accident one), there is no payment
-- to compute: NOTHING. No rounding: s 3.22(6) allows, but does not require, rounding to the nearest dollar.
GIVEN `the period` IS A `The entitlement period`
      `the pre-accident amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the post-accident amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum` IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the weekly payment before any reduction` MEANS
    IF `the period` EQUALS `not after the day of the accident` OR `the pre-accident amount` AT MOST `the post-accident amount`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (no period, or no loss: the text gives no amount)
    ELSE IF `the floor` GREATER THAN `the ceiling`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: subsections (3) and (4) conflict; fork F10)
         ELSE JUST (`the greater of` (`the smaller of` `the rated amount` `and` `the ceiling`) `and` `the floor`)
    WHERE
        `the rate` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the period`
            WHEN `the first entitlement period (weeks 1 to 13)` THEN 95%
            OTHERWISE IF `the post-accident amount` EQUALS 0 THEN 80% ELSE 85%
        `the rated amount` MEANS `the rate` TIMES (`the pre-accident amount` MINUS `the post-accident amount`)
        `the ceiling` MEANS `the maximum` MINUS `the post-accident amount`
        `the floor` MEANS `the smaller of` `the minimum` `and` `the pre-accident amount`

@export If I am entitled to weekly payments for a week, how much is the weekly payment for that week (ss 3.6-3.10, 3.22, 3.38)?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
      `a day in the week I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week of payment you are asking about
      `my pre-accident weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-accident weekly earnings in dollars (the weekly average of your gross earnings in the 12 months before the accident, as Schedule 1 clause 4 works it out, as last indexed under s 3.22)
      `my pre-accident earning capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-accident earning capacity in dollars a week (what you could earn in employment reasonably available to you before the accident; if it cannot be determined, 80% of NSW average weekly total earnings of full-time adults), as last indexed; used after week 78
      `my post-accident earning capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc Your post-accident earning capacity in dollars a week (what you can now earn: in weeks 1 to 78 in your pre-accident job; after week 78 in any employment reasonably available), 0 if none
      `my post-accident earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What you actually earn now, in dollars a week, 0 if nothing
      `the maximum weekly statutory benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum weekly statutory benefits amount in dollars that applies on the day the payment is payable: $3,853 in the Act itself, as last adjusted by the Authority's order each year
      `the contributory negligence reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage by which your weekly payments are reduced for contributory negligence after 52 weeks (fixed by the regulations, agreed with the insurer, or determined by the Commission), 0 if none
      `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your accident happened on or after the day the changes made by the Motor Accident Injuries Amendment Act 2022 commenced (the deposited text does not give that day)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my weekly payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the unreduced payment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (as for the unreduced payment)
    WHEN JUST `the amount` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the contributory negligence reduction` EQUALS 0 THEN JUST `the amount`
               IF `the day asked` `is more than` 52 `weeks after` `the day of my accident` THEN JUST (`the amount` TIMES ((100 MINUS `the contributory negligence reduction`) DIVIDED BY 100))
               IF (NOT `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident`) AND (`the day asked` `is more than` 26 `weeks after` `the day of my accident`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: the pre-2022 text)
               OTHERWISE JUST `the amount`
    WHERE
        `the day asked` MEANS `a day in the week I am asking about`
        `the period` MEANS `the entitlement period of` `the day of my accident` `the day asked`
        `the pre-accident amount` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the period`
            WHEN `after the second entitlement period (after week 78)` THEN `my pre-accident earning capacity`
            OTHERWISE `my pre-accident weekly earnings`
        `the post-accident amount` MEANS `the greater of` `my post-accident earning capacity` `and` `my post-accident earnings`
        `the unreduced payment` MEANS `the weekly payment before any reduction` `the period` `the pre-accident amount` `the post-accident amount` `the maximum weekly statutory benefits amount` `the minimum weekly statutory benefits amount`
        -- s 3.10 and Regulation cl 7: "the minimum weekly statutory benefits amount is the amount that is 2.5% of the
        -- maximum weekly statutory benefits amount".
        `the minimum weekly statutory benefits amount` MEANS `the maximum weekly statutory benefits amount` TIMES (2.5%)

§§ `s 3.38(2) -- when a finding of contributory negligence must be made`

-- s 3.38(2) "A finding of contributory negligence must be made in the following cases -- (a) where the injured person
-- has been convicted of an alcohol or other drug-related offence in relation to the motor accident, unless the injured
-- person satisfies the insurer or the Commission that the alcohol or other drug ... did not contribute in any way to
-- the accident, (b) where (i) the injured person (not being a minor) was ... a voluntary passenger ... and (ii) the
-- driver's ability to drive ... was impaired as a consequence of the consumption of alcohol or any other drug and the
-- injured person was aware, or ought to have been aware, of the impairment, unless ... the injured person could not
-- reasonably be expected to have declined to become a passenger ..., (c) where the injured person (not being a minor)
-- was ... not wearing a seat belt when required by law to do so, (d) ... not wearing a protective helmet when required
-- by law to do so, (e) where the defence of volenti non fit injuria would have been available, but for section 4.18
-- ..., (f) ... other conduct ... prescribed by the regulations". (5) other grounds are not excluded: where no listed
-- case holds, NOTHING.
@export Must a finding of contributory negligence be made against me, reducing my weekly payments after 52 weeks (s 3.38(2))?
GIVEN `I was convicted of an alcohol or drug-related driving offence for the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of an alcohol or other drug-related offence (driving with a prescribed concentration, under the influence, refusing a breath or blood test, and similar) in relation to the accident
      `I satisfied the insurer that the alcohol or drug did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have satisfied the insurer or the Commission that the alcohol or other drug did not contribute in any way to the accident
      `I was a minor at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 at the time of the accident
      `I was a voluntary passenger with a driver I knew or should have known was impaired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a voluntary passenger, the driver's ability was impaired by alcohol or another drug, and you were aware, or ought to have been aware, of it
      `I could not reasonably have declined to be a passenger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether, in the circumstances, you could not reasonably be expected to have declined to be a passenger
      `I was not wearing a seat belt when required by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were not wearing a seat belt when the law required you to
      `I was not wearing a protective helmet when required by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were not wearing a protective helmet when the law required you to
      `the defence of voluntary assumption of risk would have been available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defence of volenti non fit injuria (voluntary assumption of risk) would have been available against you in a claim for damages, but for s 4.18
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must a finding of contributory negligence be made against me` MEANS
    IF     (`I was convicted of an alcohol or drug-related driving offence for the accident` AND (NOT `I satisfied the insurer that the alcohol or drug did not contribute`))
        OR ((NOT `I was a minor at the accident`) AND `I was a voluntary passenger with a driver I knew or should have known was impaired` AND (NOT `I could not reasonably have declined to be a passenger`))
        OR ((NOT `I was a minor at the accident`) AND `I was not wearing a seat belt when required by law`)
        OR `I was not wearing a protective helmet when required by law`
        OR `the defence of voluntary assumption of risk would have been available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the list is not closed: (f) the regulations, and (5) other grounds)

§§ `s 3.19 -- notice before weekly payments stop or go down`

-- s 3.19(1) "If an injured person has received weekly payments ... for a continuous period of at least 4 weeks, the
-- insurer must not discontinue payment, or reduce the amount, ... without first giving the person not less than the
-- required period of notice". (2) 2 weeks during the first entitlement period, 4 weeks during the second, 8 weeks
-- after it. (5) not for a reduction "as a result only of" a return to work or a change in earnings; (6) not for a
-- reduction "as a result only of" a lower rate after an earlier period; (7) not for a suspension. Fork F11: (5) and (6)
-- speak of reductions only; a discontinuation for those reasons is read as covered by them too, since (4) brings in any
-- discontinuation "because the injured person ceases to be entitled". Answer: the weeks of notice, JUST 0 where none.
GIVEN `the weeks received` IS A NUMBER, `the accident day` IS A DATE, `the day of the change` IS A DATE
      `the reason` IS A `Why my weekly payments are stopping or going down`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the required period of notice in weeks` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the reason` EQUALS `I returned to or started work, or my earnings from work changed` THEN JUST 0
           IF `the reason` EQUALS `a lower rate applies because an earlier period ended` THEN JUST 0
           IF `the reason` EQUALS `my weekly payments are being suspended` THEN JUST 0
           IF `the weeks received` LESS THAN 4 THEN JUST 0
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `the entitlement period of` `the accident day` `the day of the change`
               WHEN `the first entitlement period (weeks 1 to 13)` THEN JUST 2
               WHEN `the second entitlement period (weeks 14 to 78)` THEN JUST 4
               WHEN `after the second entitlement period (after week 78)` THEN JUST 8
               OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (no payments before the accident; the text is silent)

@export How many weeks' notice must my insurer give me before it stops or reduces my weekly payments (s 3.19)?
GIVEN `the weeks I have received weekly payments without a break` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in a row you have received weekly payments up to the change
      `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
      `the day my payments stop or go down` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer stops or reduces your weekly payments
      `why they stop or go down` IS A `Why my weekly payments are stopping or going down` @desc Why. One of: "I returned to or started work, or my earnings from work changed", "a lower rate applies because an earlier period ended", "my weekly payments are being suspended", "another reason"
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How many weeks notice must my insurer give` MEANS
    `the required period of notice in weeks` `the weeks I have received weekly payments without a break` `the day of my accident` `the day my payments stop or go down` `why they stop or go down`

-- s 3.19(3) the injured person "may ... recover from the insurer an amount of statutory benefits that (a) if no period
-- of notice has been given -- is equal to the amount ... that would have been payable during the required period of
-- notice ..., or (b) if less than the required period of notice has been given -- ... during the balance of the
-- required period of notice". Both are the weeks short times the weekly amount lost.
@export If my insurer stopped or reduced my weekly payments without the notice it had to give, how much can I recover from it (s 3.19(3))?
GIVEN `the weeks I have received weekly payments without a break` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in a row you had received weekly payments up to the change
      `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
      `the day my payments stop or go down` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer stopped or reduced your weekly payments
      `why they stop or go down` IS A `Why my weekly payments are stopping or going down` @desc Why. One of: "I returned to or started work, or my earnings from work changed", "a lower rate applies because an earlier period ended", "my weekly payments are being suspended", "another reason"
      `the weeks of notice I was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks' notice of the change the insurer gave you (0 if none)
      `the weekly amount I lost` IS A NUMBER @desc How much a week, in dollars, you lost by the change (the whole weekly payment if it was stopped)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much can I recover for short notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the required period of notice in weeks` `the weeks I have received weekly payments without a break` `the day of my accident` `the day my payments stop or go down` `why they stop or go down`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (as for the required notice)
    WHEN JUST `the required weeks` THEN
        IF `the weeks of notice I was given` AT LEAST `the required weeks`
        THEN JUST 0
        ELSE JUST ((`the required weeks` MINUS `the weeks of notice I was given`) TIMES `the weekly amount I lost`)

§§ `s 3.18 -- telling the insurer about work`

-- s 3.18(1) "A person in receipt of weekly payments ... must immediately give notice to the insurer of either of the
-- following changes ... (a) the person's return to any employment or commencement of employment, (b) any change in the
-- person's earnings from any employment. Maximum penalty -- 20 penalty units." (3) not guilty if the person satisfies
-- the court that the insurer failed to inform the person of the obligation. Fork F12: no listed change, no duty (JUST
-- FALSE); not receiving weekly payments, the section does not reach the person (NOTHING).
@export Must I immediately tell my insurer that I have gone back to work or that my earnings have changed (s 3.18)?
GIVEN `I am receiving weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are receiving weekly payments of statutory benefits
      `I have returned to or started work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have returned to any employment or started employment
      `my earnings from work have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your earnings from any employment have changed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I tell my insurer about my work` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am receiving weekly payments`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a duty limited by its own wording, "A person in receipt"; the case falls outside it)
    ELSE IF `I have returned to or started work` OR `my earnings from work have changed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@export What is the most I can be fined, in penalty units, for not telling my insurer that I went back to work or my earnings changed (s 3.18)?
GIVEN `the insurer told me of this duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer told you that you must notify it of a return to work or a change in earnings (if it did not, and you satisfy the court of that, you are not guilty)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined for not telling my insurer` MEANS
    IF `the insurer told me of this duty` THEN 20 ELSE 0

§§ `Division 3.4 -- treatment and care`

-- s 3.28(1) "not entitled to statutory benefits under this Division for treatment and care expenses incurred more than
-- 52 weeks after the motor accident concerned if (a) the motor accident was caused wholly or mostly by the fault of the
-- person and the person was over 16 years of age at the time of the motor accident, or (b) the person's only injuries
-- ... were threshold injuries." "Over 16" is read as 16 or more in whole years (fork F13). Sch 4 cl 15 as for s 3.11.
-- JUST TRUE means the bar applies.
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE, `the day incurred` IS A DATE, `fault` IS A NUMBER, `age at the accident` IS A NUMBER
      `only threshold injuries` IS A BOOLEAN, `the 2022 amendments apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the s 3.28 bar` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the condition`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the day incurred` `is more than` 52 `weeks after` `the accident day` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF (NOT `the 2022 amendments apply`) AND (`the day incurred` `is more than` 26 `weeks after` `the accident day`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: the pre-2022 text)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the condition` MEANS
               (`the accident was caused wholly or mostly by my fault` `fault` AND `age at the accident` AT LEAST 16)
            OR `only threshold injuries`

-- s 3.24(1) "entitled to statutory benefits for ... (a) the reasonable cost of treatment and care, (b) reasonable and
-- necessary travel and accommodation expenses incurred by the injured person in order to obtain treatment and care
-- ..., (c) if the injured person is under the age of 18 years or otherwise requires assistance to travel ..., [those]
-- of a parent or other carer". (2) "No statutory benefits are payable ... to the extent that the treatment and care
-- concerned was not reasonable and necessary in the circumstances or did not relate to the injury". s 3.25 none for
-- gratuitous attendant care. s 3.27 none "unless the expenses are properly verified". s 3.29 none to the extent paid by
-- an insurer under a claim for damages or under bulk billing. s 3.31(2) the insurer "is not required to pay" for
-- treatment and care that does not accord with what the Guidelines approve (JUST FALSE, fork F14). s 3.32 the Division
-- "does not apply" to needs covered while a participant in the Lifetime Care and Support Scheme. s 3.33 none for
-- treatment and care outside Australia to a person who is not an Australian citizen or permanent resident. s 3.35(8):
-- if workers compensation for medical expenses (WCA Part 3 Division 3) has stopped, s 3.35 does not affect the
-- treatment and care benefits.
@export Can I get statutory benefits for this treatment and care expense (ss 3.24-3.33, 3.35(8))?
GIVEN `the accident happened in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accident happened in New South Wales
      `the accident happened on or after the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened on or after the day this Act commenced (the deposited text does not give the day; its transitional provisions point to 1 December 2017)
      `the injury was caused during the driving or a collision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was caused during the driving of a vehicle, a collision with it (or action taken to avoid one), the vehicle running out of control, or a dangerous situation caused by any of those
      `the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury arose gradually from a series of incidents rather than from one accident
      `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle had cover: a NSW green slip, an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme, Commonwealth ownership, or a right of action against the Nominal Defendant
      `the injury gives rise to a work injury claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a worker injured through the negligence of your employer (a work injury claim), other than a coal miner
      `workers compensation is payable to me for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether workers compensation under the Workers Compensation Act 1987 is payable to you for this injury
      `my role` IS A `My role in a vehicle` @desc Your part in a vehicle involved. One of: "I was the driver of a vehicle involved", "I owned a vehicle involved but was not driving it", "I was neither the owner nor the driver of a vehicle involved"
      `my share of the fault` IS A NUMBER @desc Your own share of the fault for the accident, as a percentage from 0 to 100 (your contributory negligence; 100 if it was wholly your fault)
      `that vehicle was uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you owned or drove a vehicle involved: whether it had no NSW green slip where one was required, no interstate or Commonwealth compulsory cover, and was not owned by the Commonwealth
      `I drove with the owner's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver: whether you drove with the owner's authority, or believed on reasonable grounds that you had it
      `I had reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver: whether you had any reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured
      `I have been charged with a serious driving offence related to the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with or convicted of a serious driving offence about your driving of a vehicle involved in the accident
      `the charge ended in acquittal or was discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were acquitted, or the proceedings were discontinued (other than on a plea of guilty to another serious driving offence that contributed to your injury)
      `the expense` IS A `The treatment and care expense` @desc The expense. One of: "the cost of treatment and care", "my travel and accommodation to get treatment and care", "a parent's or carer's travel and accommodation to go with me to treatment and care", "attendant care services given to me that I have not paid and need not pay for", "some other expense"
      `I am under 18 or need help to travel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a parent's or carer's travel: whether you are under 18, or otherwise need assistance to travel for treatment and care
      `it was reasonable and necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment and care (or travel) was reasonable and necessary in the circumstances, and its cost reasonable
      `it related to my injury from the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment and care related to the injury from the accident
      `the expense is verified as the Guidelines require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the expense is properly verified in accordance with the Motor Accident Guidelines
      `the treatment accords with what the Guidelines approve` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment and care accords with any treatment and care the Motor Accident Guidelines approve for the matter (yes if the Guidelines say nothing about it)
      `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
      `the day the expense was incurred` IS A DATE @desc The day the expense was incurred
      `my age at the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the day of the accident
      `my only injuries were threshold injuries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your only injuries from the accident were threshold injuries (worked out by the question "Is my injury a threshold injury"): soft tissue injuries, or psychological or psychiatric injuries that are not a recognised psychiatric illness
      `it has been paid under a damages claim or bulk billing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the expense has been paid by an insurer under a claim for damages, or paid or recovered under a bulk billing arrangement
      `I am a participant in the Lifetime Care and Support Scheme for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the need arose, you were a participant in the Lifetime Care and Support Scheme for this injury
      `it was provided outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment and care was provided outside Australia
      `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen or a permanent resident of Australia
      `workers compensation for my medical expenses has stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether workers compensation for your medical, hospital and rehabilitation expenses (Workers Compensation Act 1987, Part 3 Division 3) was payable for this injury and has stopped being payable
      `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your accident happened on or after the day the changes made by the Motor Accident Injuries Amendment Act 2022 commenced (the deposited text does not give that day)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I get statutory benefits for this treatment and care expense` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the gate` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `I am a participant in the Lifetime Care and Support Scheme for this injury` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the expense` EQUALS `attendant care services given to me that I have not paid and need not pay for` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the expense` EQUALS `a parent's or carer's travel and accommodation to go with me to treatment and care` AND (NOT `I am under 18 or need help to travel`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `it was reasonable and necessary`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `it related to my injury from the accident`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the expense is verified as the Guidelines require`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the treatment accords with what the Guidelines approve`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the s 3.28 bar` `the day of my accident` `the day the expense was incurred` `my share of the fault` `my age at the accident` `my only injuries were threshold injuries` `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `it has been paid under a damages claim or bulk billing` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `it was provided outside Australia` AND (NOT `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the s 3.28 bar` `the day of my accident` `the day the expense was incurred` `my share of the fault` `my age at the accident` `my only injuries were threshold injuries` `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: the pre-2022 text)
           IF `the expense` EQUALS `some other expense` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent on other expenses in this Division; s 3.26 covers paid domestic services)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `workers compensation bars it` MEANS `workers compensation is payable to me for the injury` AND (NOT `workers compensation for my medical expenses has stopped`)
        `the gate` MEANS `the Part 3 gate` `the accident happened in New South Wales` `the accident happened on or after the Act commenced` `the injury was caused during the driving or a collision` `the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents` `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover` `the injury gives rise to a work injury claim` `workers compensation bars it` `my role` `my share of the fault` `that vehicle was uninsured` `I drove with the owner's authority` `I had reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured` `I have been charged with a serious driving offence related to the accident` `the charge ended in acquittal or was discontinued`

-- s 3.26(1) "entitled to statutory benefits ... for the reasonable expenses incurred after the motor accident in
-- employing a person to provide domestic services to the claimant's dependants, but only if (a) [for dependants under
-- paragraph (a) of the definition] the claimant provided the services to those dependants before the motor accident,
-- and (b) the claimant's dependants were not (or will not be) capable of performing the services themselves by reason
-- of their age or physical or mental incapacity, and (c) there is a reasonable expectation that, but for the claimant's
-- injury, the claimant would have provided the services ... for at least 6 hours per week and for a period of at least
-- 6 consecutive months, and (d) there will be a need for the services ... and that need is reasonable". "Statutory
-- benefits are not so payable if the domestic services provided after the motor accident are provided gratuitously."
-- (3) none if the dependant has previously recovered damages for that loss. (4) these are treatment and care, so
-- ss 3.27 and 3.28 apply.
@export Can I get statutory benefits for paying someone to do the domestic services I used to do for my dependants (s 3.26)?
GIVEN `the accident happened in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accident happened in New South Wales
      `the accident happened on or after the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened on or after the day this Act commenced (the deposited text does not give the day; its transitional provisions point to 1 December 2017)
      `the injury was caused during the driving or a collision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was caused during the driving of a vehicle, a collision with it (or action taken to avoid one), the vehicle running out of control, or a dangerous situation caused by any of those
      `the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury arose gradually from a series of incidents rather than from one accident
      `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle had cover: a NSW green slip, an interstate or Commonwealth compulsory scheme, Commonwealth ownership, or a right of action against the Nominal Defendant
      `the injury gives rise to a work injury claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a worker injured through the negligence of your employer (a work injury claim), other than a coal miner
      `workers compensation is payable to me for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether workers compensation under the Workers Compensation Act 1987 is payable to you for this injury
      `my role` IS A `My role in a vehicle` @desc Your part in a vehicle involved. One of: "I was the driver of a vehicle involved", "I owned a vehicle involved but was not driving it", "I was neither the owner nor the driver of a vehicle involved"
      `my share of the fault` IS A NUMBER @desc Your own share of the fault for the accident, as a percentage from 0 to 100 (your contributory negligence; 100 if it was wholly your fault)
      `that vehicle was uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you owned or drove a vehicle involved: whether it had no NSW green slip where one was required, no interstate or Commonwealth compulsory cover, and was not owned by the Commonwealth
      `I drove with the owner's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver: whether you drove with the owner's authority, or believed on reasonable grounds that you had it
      `I had reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were the driver: whether you had any reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured
      `I have been charged with a serious driving offence related to the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with or convicted of a serious driving offence about your driving of a vehicle involved in the accident
      `the charge ended in acquittal or was discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were acquitted, or the proceedings were discontinued (other than on a plea of guilty to another serious driving offence that contributed to your injury)
      `the dependant` IS A `The dependant` @desc The person you provided (or would have provided) the services to. One of: "my spouse, de facto partner or relative, who depended on me at the time of the accident", "another member of my household, who depended on me at the time of the accident", "my child, unborn at the time of the accident and born after it", "none of these"
      `I provided the services to them before the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provided these domestic services to them before the accident
      `they cannot do the services themselves because of age or incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your dependants were not (or will not be) capable of doing the services themselves because of their age or physical or mental incapacity
      `the hours a week I would have provided` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week you would reasonably have been expected to provide the services but for your injury (leave out weeks of short occasional respite or other assisted care, as s 3.26(2) allows)
      `the consecutive months I would have provided them` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive months you would reasonably have been expected to provide them
      `the need for those hours and months is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there will be a need for the services for those hours and that period, and the need is reasonable in all the circumstances
      `the services are now provided for free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the services now provided after the accident are provided free of charge
      `the dependant has already recovered damages for this loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dependant has already recovered damages for the loss of your capacity to provide these services
      `the expenses are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the expenses of employing someone are reasonable
      `the expense is verified as the Guidelines require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the expense is properly verified in accordance with the Motor Accident Guidelines
      `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
      `the day the expense was incurred` IS A DATE @desc The day the expense was incurred
      `my age at the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the day of the accident
      `my only injuries were threshold injuries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your only injuries from the accident were threshold injuries (soft tissue injuries, or psychological or psychiatric injuries that are not a recognised psychiatric illness)
      `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your accident happened on or after the day the changes made by the Motor Accident Injuries Amendment Act 2022 commenced (the deposited text does not give that day)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I get statutory benefits for paid domestic services` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the gate` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the dependant` EQUALS `none of these` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `paragraph (a) dependant` AND (NOT `I provided the services to them before the accident`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `they cannot do the services themselves because of age or incapacity`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the hours a week I would have provided` LESS THAN 6 THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the consecutive months I would have provided them` LESS THAN 6 THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the need for those hours and months is reasonable`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the services are now provided for free` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the dependant has already recovered damages for this loss` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the expense is verified as the Guidelines require`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the s 3.28 bar` `the day of my accident` `the day the expense was incurred` `my share of the fault` `my age at the accident` `my only injuries were threshold injuries` `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the s 3.28 bar` `the day of my accident` `the day the expense was incurred` `my share of the fault` `my age at the accident` `my only injuries were threshold injuries` `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: the pre-2022 text)
           IF (NOT `the expenses are reasonable`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited by its own wording, "reasonable expenses"; the case falls outside it)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) dependant` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the dependant`
            WHEN `my child, unborn at the time of the accident and born after it` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the gate` MEANS `the Part 3 gate` `the accident happened in New South Wales` `the accident happened on or after the Act commenced` `the injury was caused during the driving or a collision` `the injury arose gradually from a series of incidents` `a vehicle involved had motor accident insurance cover` `the injury gives rise to a work injury claim` `workers compensation is payable to me for the injury` `my role` `my share of the fault` `that vehicle was uninsured` `I drove with the owner's authority` `I had reasonable grounds to believe the vehicle was uninsured` `I have been charged with a serious driving offence related to the accident` `the charge ended in acquittal or was discontinued`

§§ `Division 3.2 -- funeral expenses (a situation: someone has died)`

-- s 3.4(1) "If the death of a person results from a motor accident, statutory benefits are payable for reasonable
-- funeral expenses to (a) the legal personal representative of the deceased, or (b) if there is no legal personal
-- representative -- the person who has paid or is liable to pay those expenses." (4) death includes the loss of a
-- foetus. s 3.35(6) not payable "if workers compensation is paid or payable in respect of the death under Division 1 of
-- Part 3 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987". s 3.36(1) reaches the death of an at-fault owner or driver of an
-- uninsured vehicle. s 3.40(2): funeral benefits are deducted from damages recovered under the Compensation to
-- Relatives Act 1897 (not computed here).
@export Can I be paid statutory benefits for the funeral expenses of a person who died because of a motor accident (ss 3.4, 3.35(6), 3.36)?
GIVEN `the death resulted from a motor accident the Act applies to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death (including the loss of a foetus) resulted from a motor accident in New South Wales to which the Act applies
      `my position` IS A `My position after the death` @desc Your position. One of: "I am the legal personal representative of the person who died", "I paid or must pay the funeral expenses, and there is no legal personal representative", "I paid or must pay the funeral expenses, but there is a legal personal representative", "none of these"
      `the funeral expenses are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the funeral expenses are reasonable
      `workers compensation is paid or payable for the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether workers compensation is paid or payable for the death under Division 1 of Part 3 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987
      `the person who died was mostly at fault as owner or driver of an uninsured vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was the owner or driver of an uninsured vehicle and the accident was wholly or mostly (more than 61%) their fault, and they were not a driver protected by s 3.36(5) (driving with authority, with no reason to think the vehicle uninsured)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I get statutory benefits for funeral expenses` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the death resulted from a motor accident the Act applies to`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `workers compensation is paid or payable for the death` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the person who died was mostly at fault as owner or driver of an uninsured vehicle` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `my position` EQUALS `I paid or must pay the funeral expenses, but there is a legal personal representative` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `my position` EQUALS `none of these` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the text lists recipients without "only")
           IF (NOT `the funeral expenses are reasonable`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited by its own wording, "reasonable funeral expenses")
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 3.4(2) a deceased who usually lived in Australia: funeral expenses include the reasonable cost of transporting the
-- body to "(a) what would ... be an appropriate place for its preparation for burial or cremation, (b) that usual place
-- of residence"; (3) a deceased who usually lived in another country: "the reasonable cost of transporting the body
-- ... to that country". (5) a foetus's usual place of residence is the pregnant woman's. "Include": another journey is
-- NOTHING.
@export Do the funeral expenses include the cost of transporting the body to this place (s 3.4(2), (3), (5))?
GIVEN `the person who died usually lived in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died usually lived in Australia when they died (for a foetus, where the pregnant woman usually lived)
      `where the body is taken` IS A `Where the body is taken` @desc Where the body is taken. One of: "an appropriate place to prepare it for burial or cremation", "the usual place of residence of the person who died", "the country outside Australia where the person who died usually lived", "somewhere else"
      `the transport cost is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cost of the transport is reasonable
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do funeral expenses include transporting the body there` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the transport cost is reasonable`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited by its own wording, "reasonable cost")
    ELSE IF `the person who died usually lived in Australia`
         THEN CONSIDER `where the body is taken`
              WHEN `an appropriate place to prepare it for burial or cremation` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `the usual place of residence of the person who died` THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind ("include": the text does not close the list)
         ELSE CONSIDER `where the body is taken`
              WHEN `the country outside Australia where the person who died usually lived` THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind ("include": the text does not close the list)
